WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.202
-My first guest is
an Oscar-winning actress

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:06.806
who stars in the Hulu series
"Nine Perfect Strangers."

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.041
The finale begins streaming
tomorrow.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:12.345
Here is the one and only
Nicole Kidman!

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.248
Oh, my goodness. Come on now.

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.284
Oh!

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.987
Ah, so happy to see you, Nicole.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.522
You look gorgeous, pal.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.057
Thank you so much
for coming to see us.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.391
I appreciate this.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.326
-I wish I was there in person.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.894
-I know. Well, next time.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.529
Next time, you're going to be,
I know it.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:32.064
I know it's gonna happen.
-I will come in. Yes, I will.

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.199
-I know you love New York

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.468
and it's a very special place
for you.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.236
You got engaged here,
I know that.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.372
I know -- Didn't you?

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.741
Yeah. Do I know that?
-You're not meant to know that.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.975
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.444
-Yeah, I'm allowed to know
all the stuff.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.379
I know all sorts of stuff
about you.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.649
When did you first -- when did
you first -- did Keith Urban

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.984
just sweep you off your feet?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.853
When did you know?

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:58.224
-He sat on the stoop
of my New York apartment.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.894
I came out 5:00 a.m.
in the morning,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.196
and it was my birthday
and he had flowers.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.097
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.665
And that was it.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.433
I was a goner.
-That's how you do it.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.968
-I'm like,
"Yes, I'll marry you."

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.103
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.904
And you just celebrated
15 years, right?

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.572
Your 15th anniversary?
Congratulations.

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:16.409
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.278
For a second there, I thought
you said 50 years.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.115
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Going back in time.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.916
-Hopefully, one day.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.753
-But, yeah, 15 years, which is
pretty amazing, right?

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.454
-It's the greatest.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:32.325
-Did you do any party
or any surprises --

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.160
No, you don't like surprises.
I know this.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.361
-No.
-I know this.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.996
I don't like surprises either.
-No, I do not.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.230
-Why not?
-You don't?

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.466
-No, I really do not --
-I mean, I don't mind

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:44.604
a surprise,
like something kind of sweet,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.239
but I don't like
a surprise party.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.908
It's too -- I had
a surprise party once

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.511
and I broke out in a cold sore
on the spot from the shock.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.380
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.050
I literally did.
It was too stressful.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.786
It was like I was seeing --
It was apparitions.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.921
It was bizarre.
I didn't like it at all.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.656
-Every now and then, I like
a surprise, but not a big --

00:02:04.656 --> 00:02:06.325
it has to be a small one.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.994
I feel like it's like I'm
tricking someone or something

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:11.397
and I don't like to do that,
so I feel weird --

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.366
I don't like surprises.
I like to know what's happening.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.668
I'll act surprised.
-Yes.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.302
Yes, we know that.

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:23.275
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:27.146
Did I just burn you?
[ Laughs ]

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:31.017
-Would you ever -- Because I've
seen you sing with Keith before.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.352
Would you guys ever
do a duet album?

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.154
-No. No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.089
-Why? Why?

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.425
-Because you have to --
I mean, I have this thing

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.161
where just stay in your lane,
right?

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.363
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.231
I shouldn't be trying to get
into his lane.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.300
I'm fine where I am.
-Okay, yeah. Okay, yeah.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.335
-So yeah.
-So it would never happen.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:53.205
-And also I just -- I don't feel
comfortable singing.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:58.644
I have sung but it's not really
what I feel comfortable doing.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.813
-So you wouldn't perform
in front of crowds

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.149
like Keith plays
arenas and stuff.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.950
Yeah, he goes on tour,
and he's amazing.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.853
-Yes, he's playing Vegas
right now.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.621
-Is he really?
He's unbelievable.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.924
-Which is why I couldn't be
with you because I chose him.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:16.195
I mean, in terms of the Vegas
and it's -- Yeah, to be here.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:19.031
-Would you --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.166
-Shut up, Nicole.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.902
-Dude, I can't even write this,
I swear.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.805
I can't write this.
What are we doing?

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.639
-What are we doing?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:29.608
Ask me something good.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.377
-I will. Come on.
-Sorry.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.379
-I am. I will.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.981
Just stop it.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:38.317
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:39.518
-Now I'm like, "What?"

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:42.888
-Just chill out.
Just calm down for two seconds.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:46.559
Gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:50.663
Nicole, I want to talk to you
about what you're amazing at,

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:53.499
which is acting, and you're also
producing "Nine --"

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, really, every single day

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.838
you come out with -- It's like
you just keep proving yourself,

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.673
and you're like, "Oh, okay,
she's the greatest."

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.709
It's another one
that's a slam dunk.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.511
"Nine Perfect Strangers." It's
the new "it" show right now.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.013
It's on Hulu.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.049
People love it.
Everyone's talking about it.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.717
-Yes.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.320
-The finale streams tomorrow.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.356
Can you set up what
the show is about?

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.059
-This show is
such a trippy ride.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.627
-Yeah, it is.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:25.131
-Nine strangers check into
a wellness retreat,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.666
which is run by me.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:32.205
-I play a Russian-American
woman, and her name is Masha.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:36.743
-Yeah.
-And we treat the people

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:41.246
for their depression or their
trauma or any of the things

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:43.816
that they're going through, and
it's sort of this crazy ride.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:47.920
And the finale happens to be
my favorite episode.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.388
-Oh, really?

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.357
-Yeah, so that's kind of good.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.392
But it gets crazy.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:55.628
It all goes down
in episode eight.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.630
-I heard that you stayed in
character the whole time,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.131
by the way.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.801
-I did actually,
which was really weird

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:05.404
because the other actors, I only
met them on the first day,

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:10.142
and I had met Melissa previously
and Bobby,

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:14.079
but I never really gotten to
know anybody in the cast,

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:17.416
which was kind of great,
so I just stayed as this

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:23.022
Russian woman and related to
everybody through my character.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.090
-Wow.
-And it was actually weird

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.361
because I didn't get to
really know them as Nicole.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.895
I got to know them as Masha,

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:34.567
and on the final day, a number
of the people were like,

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.568
"Gosh, we've never even heard
you speak

00:05:36.568 --> 00:05:39.005
in your Australian accent."
-Wow.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:42.542
-I would go up and hug them
and I would stroke them.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.611
[ Laughter ]
And I would stroke their hair

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.613
and listen to their stories,
yeah.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.982
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Nicole Kidman

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.384
in the finale of
"Nine Perfect Strangers."

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:53.619
Take a look at this.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.055
-Who are you?

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.823
-Who am I, Heather?

00:05:57.823 --> 00:06:02.394 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:05.998
I am a person who had somebody
who was at their center,

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:10.136
and when I lost her, I lost me.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.472
I am a person
who is living her life

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:19.112
defined by grief
and pain and loss.

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.780
I am you.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.817
I am you.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.655
I am you.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.524
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.858
-Come on!

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:35.694
Every single time,
you are phenomenal.

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:38.130
The finale of
"Nine Perfect Strangers"

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.899
begins streaming tomorrow.

